; The dependency's contract, COMMITTED rather than pinned as a flake input.
;
; There is no `stub_target` module anywhere in this tree and there must not be:
; what the outbound door has to be tested against is a target that ANSWERS, and
; the node harness in tests/test-web-variant.nix is that target. A real module
; here would drag a second build into a test about a message on a wire.
;
; `dependency_overrides` in metadata.json is the supported way to say so — it is
; the documented escape hatch for depending on something that publishes no
; contract of its own.
module stub_target {
  version "1.0.0"
  description "A target that exists only as a contract; the test harness answers for it."
  category "testing"
  depends []

  method increment(amount: int) -> int
}
